{
  "id": "COMPOUND:16120 - PROTEIN:5028",
  "verbalization": "Mono-O-Demethylcurcumin is implicated in the biological activity of COLO-824 through a series of interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Mono-O-Demethylcurcumin acts as a target for multiple receptors, including Macrophage scavenger receptor types I and II, which are in turn targets of other compounds such as Lupinine and (-)-Dicentrine. These compounds, in turn, have a shared target of COLO-824. The integration of these relationships implies a potential mechanism where Mono-O-Demethylcurcumin may influence COLO-824 through the activation of macrophage scavenger receptors, which could modulate cellular processes in the cancer cell line. The presence of multiple targets and the consistent involvement of macrophage scavenger receptors suggest a possible role in immune modulation or cellular signaling pathways. The evidence supports a hypothesis that Mono-O-Demethylcurcumin may interact with COLO-824 via a receptor-mediated mechanism, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated.",
